{"name":"Egg Noodle","hex":"#f1e3bd","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"egg noodle","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various noodles made from a mixture of egg and flour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/egg_noodle"}],"entries":[{"title":"Noodle","blocks":[{"text":"Noodles are a type of food typically made from unleavened dough which is rolled flat and cut, stretched, or extruded into long strips or strings. Noodles are a staple food in many cultures and made into a variety of shapes. The most common noodles are those derived from Chinese cuisine or Italian cuisine. Italian noodles are generally referred to as pasta. In Chinese cuisine, the overarching term for noodles is 麵, which refers specifically to dough-based noodles made from wheat or other grain-based dough. Chinese noodles also include another category, called 粉 (fěn), which are not made by kneading dough but from a starch slurry, such as rice noodles, and cellophane noodles. These are not made from wheat dough, but are still regarded as noodles in English due to their physical form and culinary role."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Dalian_Liaoning_China_Noodlemaker-01.jpg/330px-Dalian_Liaoning_China_Noodlemaker-01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Noodle","wikidata":"Q192874"},{"title":"Egg","blocks":[{"text":"An egg is an organic vessel grown by an animal to carry a possibly fertilized egg cell – a zygote. Within the vessel, an embryo is incubated until it has developed enough to survive on its own, at which point the animal hatches. Reproductive structures similar to the egg in other kingdoms are termed \"spores\", or in spermatophytes \"seeds\", or in gametophytes \"egg cells\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Adolphe_Millot_oeufs-fixed.jpg/330px-Adolphe_Millot_oeufs-fixed.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Egg","wikidata":"Q17147"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Bun_thit_nuong.jpg/500px-Bun_thit_nuong.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Bun_thit_nuong.jpg/1280px-Bun_thit_nuong.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Bun_thit_nuong.jpg/500px-Bun_thit_nuong.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A bowl of Bún thịt nướng","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABun_thit_nuong.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Vermeer_van_Utrecht_Man_eating_noodels.JPG/500px-Vermeer_van_Utrecht_Man_eating_noodels.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Vermeer_van_Utrecht_Man_eating_noodels.JPG/500px-Vermeer_van_Utrecht_Man_eating_noodels.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Jan Vermeer van Utrecht's painting of a man eating unspecified noodles (National Museum, Warsaw)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVermeer_van_Utrecht_Man_eating_noodels.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Pasta_2006_5.jpg/330px-Pasta_2006_5.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Pasta_2006_5.jpg/960px-Pasta_2006_5.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Pasta_2006_5.jpg/330px-Pasta_2006_5.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A